# SPDX-License-Identifier: CC0-1.0
# =============================================================================
# PHP2Shell: audit every program the web-server account starts  (v1)
# CVE-2026-109618 / CVE-2026-109619
#
# If this software is helpful, consider a donation to our 501c3 nonprofit:
# https://privacysafe.foundation
#
# DETECTION, NOT PREVENTION, AND NOT A FIX. The only complete fix is a patched
# PHP (8.5.12 / 8.4.27 / 8.3.36 / 8.2.35, or your distribution's backport).
#
# Report: https://github.com/0x4D31/honeypot-data/blob/main/reports/php2shell/2026-10-24-confirmed-rce.md
#
# The strongest evidence in the 24 October 2026 phpot honeypot report was process-level:
# an Apache worker starting /bin/sh as uid 33. Logs only show the residue, and
# the phpot report's final request never reached the access log because the worker
# died. php2shell-watch.sh polls /proc once a second and can miss a shell that
# starts and exits between samples. Auditing execve does not: the kernel
# records every program the account starts, with its parent PID, executable
# and arguments.
#
# Install (needs the auditd package):
#   cp php2shell-auditd.rules /etc/audit/rules.d/60-php2shell.rules
#   augenrules --load
#   auditctl -l | grep php2shell_web_exec
# Review:
#   ausearch -k php2shell_web_exec -ts today -i
#   php2shell-mitigate.sh hunt        (5.2.0 and later reads this key)
# Remove: delete the file, then augenrules --load.
#
# Edit the uid. 33 is www-data on Debian, Ubuntu and Trisquel (id -u www-data).
# A PHP-FPM pool that runs as another account needs its own line; read each
# pool's "user =" setting. Containers: audit rules run on the host and match
# the numeric uid, which is the same inside the container unless it uses user
# namespaces.
#
# Expect some noise where the application legitimately runs programs
# (ImageMagick, sendmail, git). Review a week of it first. To silence a known
# harmless program, put a "never" rule for it BEFORE the rules below, for
# example:
#   -a never,exit -F arch=b64 -S execve -F euid=33 -F exe=/usr/bin/convert
# =============================================================================

# auid 4294967295 is "unset": a daemon, not a login session.
-a always,exit -F arch=b64 -S execve -F euid=33 -F auid=4294967295 -k php2shell_web_exec

# 32-bit programs, on systems that run them. Some kernels reject b32 rules, so
# this one is off by default.
#-a always,exit -F arch=b32 -S execve -F euid=33 -F auid=4294967295 -k php2shell_web_exec

# Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
